		<title type="html"><![CDATA[MD-9600 Analog FM Audio reports of overdriven/fuzzy]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3178&amp;p=25491#p25491"><![CDATA[
On the MD-9600 running OpenGD DMR audio has good reports of audio coming back.<br><br>Over on Analog FM side. I've gotten quite a few reports recently of the mic sounding fuzzy and overdriven. I turn the mic  gain down from 0db to anything lower, then it sounds too quiet.<br><br>Anyone else been having this issue? I bought a replacement mic thinking that was it, but a friend has the same exact issue on his radio running OpenGD<br><br>It sounds better on FM if you hold the mic further away, so maybe that's it? It's the same place I hold my other mics, but that doesn't mean anything!<br><br><br>Curious to see if anyone else has had this issue, or if a fix could be found?<br><br><br>Thanks for all the hard work on this software, it's awesome to have a base radio have the same codeplug and software as HTs!<br><br><br>I'm currently running 8.18 release, about to update to the new 8.21 release. I've also seen this on older betas when I tested it, like Feb's release.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4334">KD2YFY</a> — Mon Aug 21, 2023 10:28 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
